        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Upon the stars, that is where the talent and intellect reside. Oblivious to the world, as the envy becomes blinding."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Who knew gentleness and kindness welcomed only pain and suffering. Like the risk of falling into the depths when trying to mount the sky."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "An inquiry into spirit traces, a glance into the site of storage. Even with iron shoes worn out unearthly, one has to visit the three depths."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Better off alone than to be an accomplice. One day, as they turn around, a path will be lit by the radiance of the stars."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-89556328dae6cc96"
          },
          {
